course: dictionary
lesson: 15455
title: Stimulate: making things more active
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To stimulate something means to make it more active, or to make it grow or work better. Look at the words around it: «Exercise stimulates your heart» tells you that exercise makes your heart work harder.
explain: With people, stimulate means to make them interested, excited or full of ideas. «The trip stimulated my interest in rocks» means the trip made me more interested in rocks. Try your meaning in the sentence: "made" fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: In science, stimulate means to make a nerve or a sense react. «Light stimulates the eye» means light makes the eye respond. The words around stimulate tell you whether it is about a body, a person or an idea.
fact: Stimulate is a verb: stimulate, stimulates, stimulated, stimulating.
fact: «Stimulate» means to make something more active, grow or work more.
fact: «Stimulate» with a person means to make them interested, excited or full of ideas.
fact: In biology, «stimulate» means to make a nerve or sense react, as light stimulates the eye.
fact: Phrases you may meet: stimulate interest, stimulate growth, stimulating conversation.
exercise: «Exercise stimulates your heart.» What does stimulates mean here? | Gives your heart a long rest | Makes your heart smaller | Makes your heart stop | *Makes your heart more active
exercise: «The trip stimulated my interest in rocks.» What does stimulated mean? | Made me bored of rocks | *Made me more interested in rocks | Stopped me from seeing rocks | Gave me a new pair of boots
exercise: In science, what does light stimulate? | A rock | A cup | *The eye | The river bank
test: «Teachers want to stimulate discussion in class.» What do teachers want to do? | Write a long list of rules | Make the room darker | *Make pupils excited to talk and share ideas | Stop everyone from talking
test: «Sunshine stimulates the plants to grow.» What does stimulates mean? | *Makes them grow more actively | Covers them up | Makes them lose their colour | Makes them fall over
exam: Which word means to make someone interested and full of ideas? | hide | *stimulate | empty | sleep
